WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.496 --> 00:00:15.500
Holes mark ground inside a region where the mobs never go: trees, rocks, water. The server never spawns a mob in a hole, so a hole that is too small lets one spawn inside a tree.

2
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:23.704
This is Jugner Forest. Select the region, here west seventy-six, and find the hole. Hovering it shows its size.

3
00:00:23.704 --> 00:00:35.507
The dots circle it, but stop a good way short of its edge. Nothing was ever recorded in that gap, so the tree is wider than the hole.

4
00:00:35.507 --> 00:00:59.406
Drag the hole's corners outward, the same way as an outline's: a whole side at a time, stopping just short of the dots.

5
00:00:59.406 --> 00:01:06.409
Or let the editor size it. Right-click inside the hole and choose Grow to roam data.

6
00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:20.609
The preview grows the hole over all the ground around it that no mob walked on. Clearance keeps its edge that far from the nearest recorded step; a larger clearance gives a smaller hole.

7
00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:24.403
Apply cuts it.

8
00:01:24.403 --> 00:01:33.809
The same right-click menu deletes a hole, or merges it with the holes around it. And Control Z undoes any of it.
